The user is asking why we need a debug build instead of being able to use the release build. Let me explain the reason clearly.

Looking at the source code we found in `MobileHostService.swift`:

```swift
#if !DEBUG
// Release builds never advertise a loopback route (the 127.0.0.1
// `debugLoopback` route is DEBUG-only, see `MobileRouteResolver`), so a
// legitimate phone always reaches the Mac over the Tailscale interface.
// A connection arriving on loopback in release can only be a local
// process (or a browser that somehow framed the binary protocol), never
```

Security purposes, since a legitimate phone should never appear as a loopback connection—only the emulator does that. This explains why the debug build is required for Android emulator testing while a real device would work fine with the release build over Tailscale.

